WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.420
Marcus is applying for a life policy.

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.000
The producer asks the questions on the approved application, records his

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.460
answers and gathers the requested supporting facts.

4
00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:13.940
This is field underwriting.

5
00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:18.220
It helps the insurer evaluate the risk, but it does not

6
00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:21.400
give the producer unlimited authority to approve coverage.

7
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.960
The producer's report records relevant observations and transaction

8
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:30.720
information truthfully. A blank answer is not automatically a no.

9
00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:35.340
An unfamiliar medication is not a diagnosis the agent should invent.

10
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.680
Ask for clarification and follow the carrier's approved procedure.

11
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:47.040
Explain that underwriting and any temporary protection depend on their

12
00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:51.474
actual requirements. Elena notices that the application lists the wrong

13
00:00:51.474 --> 00:00:56.134
medication date. Correct it through the insurer's approved process and obtain

14
00:00:56.134 --> 00:01:01.034
the required acknowledgment. Never erase a material answer secretly after

15
00:01:01.034 --> 00:01:04.054
signature or ask a client to sign a blank form for

16
00:01:04.054 --> 00:01:09.034
later completion. Verify the proposed insured, owner and other required

17
00:01:09.034 --> 00:01:11.334
signatures and each person's authority.

18
00:01:12.214 --> 00:01:16.194
When more than one person completes a Maryland application, the signature

19
00:01:16.194 --> 00:01:19.794
area must identify the portion to which each signature applies.

20
00:01:20.874 --> 00:01:24.354
A lawful electronic signature process can be used when accepted.

21
00:01:25.134 --> 00:01:28.114
Convenience does not authorize signing someone else's name.

22
00:01:29.028 --> 00:01:33.168
Maryland treats statements in a life application as representations,

23
00:01:34.108 --> 00:01:38.748
not warranties. Health questions must use the applicant's knowledge and

24
00:01:38.748 --> 00:01:42.588
belief standard or include the required representation statement.

25
00:01:43.248 --> 00:01:45.528
That does not make false answers harmless.

26
00:01:46.588 --> 00:01:51.228
Under Maryland law, a fraudulent or material misstatement can affect

27
00:01:51.228 --> 00:01:56.008
recovery, and the statute also considers whether correct facts would have

28
00:01:56.008 --> 00:02:01.228
changed the insurer's good-faith decision to issue, price or cover the

29
00:02:01.228 --> 00:02:05.428
risk. Do not teach that fraud is the only possible problem.

30
00:02:06.328 --> 00:02:10.608
An agent should record the truth and refer an uncertain answer

31
00:02:10.608 --> 00:02:14.748
for clarification, not coach the applicant to hide it.

32
00:02:15.606 --> 00:02:19.886
The applicant should understand what information may be collected, how it

33
00:02:19.886 --> 00:02:23.506
may be used and the rights described in the applicable notice.

34
00:02:24.366 --> 00:02:28.926
Giving an information-practices notice is not the same as obtaining every

35
00:02:28.926 --> 00:02:33.826
required authorization. A consumer report containing medical information

36
00:02:33.826 --> 00:02:38.306
requires the applicant's permission before the reporting agency provides it.

37
00:02:38.826 --> 00:02:44.286
If underwriting calls for an HIV test, use the appropriate informed-consent

38
00:02:44.286 --> 00:02:49.426
and confidentiality process rather than treating an ordinary signature as

39
00:02:49.426 --> 00:02:51.006
permission for every test.

40
00:02:52.046 --> 00:02:53.546
Explain the current carrier forms.

41
00:02:54.546 --> 00:02:58.766
Collect only relevant information through authorized channels and protect it

42
00:02:58.766 --> 00:03:03.900
from unnecessary disclosure. An applicant wants a large cash-value

43
00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:08.580
policy, seems unconcerned about protection and asks how quickly an unrelated

44
00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:11.120
person can receive a surrender payment.

45
00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:16.080
This combination calls for the insurer's anti-money-laundering review.

46
00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:21.460
The federal insurance rule focuses on covered products, including individual

47
00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:27.120
permanent life and individual annuities, with the stated cash-value and

48
00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:32.440
investment features. It does not impose an identical rule on every

49
00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:37.620
insurance product. The insurer must integrate relevant agents and brokers

50
00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:42.880
into its program. Follow training, identity and

51
00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:47.900
customer-information procedures, document the facts and escalate concerns.

52
00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:52.700
Do not promise confidentiality that would defeat a required report.

53
00:03:53.634 --> 00:03:58.694
Before submission, check the plan, amount, riders, ownership,

54
00:03:59.294 --> 00:04:04.154
beneficiary information, answers, signatures, notices and any premium

55
00:04:04.154 --> 00:04:08.954
receipt. Tell Marcus what additional underwriting evidence may be needed.

56
00:04:09.854 --> 00:04:13.154
A submitted application is not the same as an issued policy

57
00:04:13.154 --> 00:04:15.614
or a promise of immediate coverage.

58
00:04:16.194 --> 00:04:20.914
If a consumer report contributes to an adverse decision, the required

59
00:04:20.914 --> 00:04:26.054
notice identifies the reporting agency and explains the consumer's report

60
00:04:26.054 --> 00:04:31.494
and dispute rights. The reporting agency did not make the insurer's

61
00:04:31.494 --> 00:04:35.874
decision. Help the applicant follow the review process while protecting

62
00:04:35.874 --> 00:04:41.534
privacy. Never solve a disappointing result by changing facts or

63
00:04:41.534 --> 00:04:42.734
hiding another application.
